 * Rounds towards "nearest neighbor" unless both neighbors are equidistant, in which case round up.
 *
 * Behaves as for Up if the discarded fraction is >= 0.5; otherwise, behaves as for Down.
 * Note that this is the rounding mode commonly taught at school.
 *
 * Equivalent native PHP rounding mode: {@see \RoundingMode::HalfAwayFromZero}.
 */";s:9:"startLine";i:71;s:7:"endLine";i:71;s:11:"startColumn";i:5;s:9:"endColumn";i:16;}s:8:"HalfDown";a:8:{s:4:"name";s:8:"HalfDown";s:5:"value";N;s:10:"attributes";a:0:{}s:10:"docComment";s:283:"/**
 * Rounds towards "nearest neighbor" unless both neighbors are equidistant, in which case round down.
 *
